According to a report by Intel Market Research, Global air ambulance services market was valued at USD 7.2 billion in 2025, reflecting a substantial rise driven by an expanding demand for time critical patient transport. The market is projected to grow from USD 7.4 billion in 2026 to USD 10.1 billion by 2034, exhibiting a CAGR of 4.3% during the forecast period.
Air ambulance services comprise medically equipped aircraft-fixed wing jets or helicopters-staffed by critical care physicians and nurses who transport patients requiring urgent care across long distances or challenging terrain. Advanced life support systems, telemedicine connectivity and specialised handling protocols enable the maintenance of clinical stability during flight.
